  "Question": "\\(y\\) varies inversely as the square of \\(x.\\) When \\(y=16,\\) \\(x=1.\\) When \\(x=8,\\) \\(y\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(128\\)",
    "C": "\\(64\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac14\\)",
    "E": "\\(1024\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Inverse variation with the square of \\(x\\) means that \\(yx^2=k\\) is constant, with \\(x\\ne0\\). The given values determine\n\\[\nk=16\\cdot1^2=16.\n\\]\nTherefore, when \\(x=8\\),\n\\[\ny=\\frac{16}{8^2}=\\frac{16}{64}=\\frac14.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac14}\\), choice D.",
